        "description": "**Overview**<br><br>\n  The Update White Labelling Configuration API enables authorized users to modify existing white-labelling settings for DNS domains or channels. \n  This allows partners or channels to update branding, themes, notification templates, and API host configurations.\n  This API supports both full and partial updates, ensuring flexibility in maintaining the white-labelling without having to overwrite the existing values.\n\n---\n\n**Key Features**\n  - **Granular Updates:** Supports updating specific sections within a configuration without having to replace the entire configuration.\n  - **Domain and Channel Level:** Allows updates on DNS domain and channel level based on token permissions.\n  - **Dynamic Branding:** Enables real-time changes to logos, colors, fonts, and email templates.\n  - **API Host Management:** Supports modification of API host URLs as part of branding updates.\n\n---\n\n**Purpose and Use Cases**\n  - Allows a channel to update a DNS domain configuration under its ownership.\n  - Enables channels to configure their own channel-level branding settings, such as custom email templates for application events.\n  - Allows updates on channel level in case where it is overriding the DNS domain-level configuration.\n\n  ---\n\n**Expected Outcomes**\n  - The white-labelling configuration is updated successfully with the new settings.\n  - Updated branding and settings propagate to all associated applications, portals, and notifications reflecting the changes dynamically.\n",
