        "summary": "Delete a white-labelling configuration",
        "description": "**Overview** <br><br>\n  The Delete White Labelling Configuration API endpoint allows authorized users to remove a specific white-labelling configuration by its unique identifier. This operation permanently deletes the configuration settings associated with a channel or partner, effectively reverting any custom branding or theming applied through that configuration.\n\n---\n\n**Key Features**\n  - **Targeted Deletion**: Removes a single white-labelling configuration based on its unique ID.\n  - **Permission Enforcement**: Ensures only users with valid channel access tokens and ownership of the configuration can delete it.\n  - **Fallback Behaviour**: After deletion, the system automatically reverts to the applicable parent configuration (channel or root) based on the scope of the access token.\n  - **Clean Removal**: Ensures the removal of all associated branding and customization details from the system.\n\n---\n\n**Constraints on deletion**\n  - If a channel-level configuration overrides a DNS domain-level configuration, the DNS-level configuration cannot be deleted until the overriding configuration is removed.\n\n--- \n\n**Expected Outcomes**\n  - Successful deletion of the specified white-labelling configuration along with a confirmation response.\n  - All associated settings are removed, and fallback configurations apply automatically.\n",
